menu "Boost Gauge"

config BOOST_TPMS_BLE_ENABLED
    bool "OBD2 BLE central (TPMS + mode-01 PIDs)"
    default y
    help
        Compile the NimBLE BLE-central transport that talks to a serial-UART
        OBD-II adapter (vLinker FD+ and other ELM327-over-GATT adapters) for
        the TPMS page and generic mode-01 PIDs.

        Disable to build a BLE-less image that omits the NimBLE controller and
        host entirely. Runtime on/off of the link is a separate persisted
        setting (tpmsBle, default off) exposed on the web dashboard; flipping
        it starts/stops the BLE central without a reboot.

        NOTE: TPMS data needs the vehicle UDS DID read path, which requires a
        verified adapter profile (the research/2026-08-09 vLinker GATT profile
        doc). Keep this OFF for a pure-bench release until the link is verified
        against a real adapter.

endmenu
